The DLSS depth (0161) comes from the first resolve after depth was written, once between depth clears; color still
comes from every resolve after scene draws, so the last one wins. MUA1 resolves each predicated tile twice, and the
draws between cover the whole tile with depth at the clear value, so the second resolve gave DLSS the clear value
everywhere. A frame that writes no depth takes what the EDRAM holds at the first resolve after each clear.
scene::ScenePlanes holds the rule. Builds on 0162.

